// 015.6 (D34, #62): `Use m(...) As pfx From <CLAUSE>` grounds every rule instantiated by the
// module against `<CLAUSE>`, allowing standard-library modules under `--require-provenance`.
//! require-provenance
Document "include/byref_doc.md"

Module mini-escrow(holder, beneficiary, amount) {
  Function held Identified by beneficiary * amount
  Act deposit Actor holder Recipient beneficiary Related to amount
    Holds when amount > 0
    Creates held(beneficiary, amount)
}

Fact landlord Identified by Lou
Fact tenant Identified by Tess
Fact usd Identified by Money(USD, 2)

Clause 1.1 Approved "a83478129c1d2d3880a6b3d7aa9aecc9057f815411df5244edcc1aba5b1d3680" Definition
Clause 1.2/1 Approved "3afb3b028233a24ca1fa6984c2bddae1a561b94cfb6d322e2cf7efd7f664fd71"
Clause 1.2/2 Approved "b576c1b03bd41c4e7217b5c2038a0c74173c78d39f3f315e8c2d32dde86ad092"
Clause 1.3 Approved "469ec0b1f9888d3dfb5ce1f0622e318f1a7e8f4508faa0081c9e487eba8dfe61"

Use mini-escrow(landlord, tenant, usd) As esc From 1.2/1
.
esc-deposit(Lou, Tess, 5000).
?esc-held(Tess, 5000).
